{"page_content": "PROC8a Transfer of substance or Covers general transferring operations of large mixture (charging and quantities of chemicals from/to vessels, containers, discharging) at non- installations or machinery without dedicated dedicated facilities 26 engineering controls in place for reducing exposure. Transfer includes loading, filling, dumping, bagging and weighing. PROC8b Transfer of substance or Covers general transferring operations from/to mixture (charging and vessels or containers with provision of dedicated discharging) at dedicated engineering controls in place for reducing exposure: facilities26 it addresses operations where material transfers are undertaken at locations that are specifically designed and operated for the transfer of larger quantities (tens of kilos and higher) of chemicals and where the exposure is primarily related to the un-coupling/coupling activity rather than the transfer itself. Such situations include tanker loading bays and drum filling. Transfer includes loading, filling, dumping, bagging. PROC9 Transfer of substance or Filling lines specifically designed to both capture mixture into small vapour and aerosol emissions and minimise containers (dedicated spillage. filling line, including weighing) This PROC can also be used to cover sampling operations. PROC10 Roller application or This includes application of paints, coatings, brushing removers, adhesives or cleaning agents to surfaces with potential exposure arising from splashes. This PROC can also be assigned to tasks such as cleaning of surfaces using long-handle tools.", "metadata": {"doc_id": "1eb9a592-eb8e-49d6-b125-40f52335ee3f", "content_type": "Table", "filename": "information_requirements_r12_en.pdf"}}